// Title: Service Binary in User Controlled Folder
// Sigma ID: 277dc340-0540-42e7-8efb-5ff460045e07
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-05-02 | Modified: 2024-03-25
// ATT&CK: persistence, defense-impairment, T1112
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects the setting of the "ImagePath" value of a service registry key to a path controlled by a
//   non-administrator user such as "\AppData\" or "\ProgramData\". Attackers often use such
//   directories for staging purposes. This rule might also trigger on badly written software, where
//   if an attacker controls an auto starting service, they might achieve persistence or privilege
//   escalation. Note that while ProgramData is a user controlled folder, software might apply strict
//   ACLs which makes them only accessible to admin users. Remove such folders via filters if you
//   experience a lot of noise.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1562.001/T1562.001.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-threat-hunting/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_service_image_path_user_controlled_folder.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where ((RegistryKey contains "ControlSet" and RegistryKey endswith "\\Services*") and RegistryKey endswith "\\ImagePath" and (RegistryValueData contains ":\\ProgramData\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\AppData\\Local\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\AppData\\Roaming\\")) and (not(((RegistryKey endswith "\\Services\\WinDefend*" or RegistryKey contains "\\Services\\MpKs") and RegistryValueData contains "C:\\ProgramData\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\"))) and (not(((RegistryKey contains "\\Services\\ZoomCptService" and RegistryValueData contains "C:\\Program Files\\Common Files\\Zoom\\Support\\CptService.exe") or (RegistryKey contains "\\Services\\MBAMInstallerService" and (RegistryValueData contains "C:\\Users\\" and RegistryValueData contains "AppData\\Local\\Temp\\MBAMInstallerService.exe")))))
